Write $I_E=\iint_{E} f(x,y)\,\mathrm{d}A$ for any subregion $E$. By additivity, recover the missing contributions:

$$
\begin{aligned}
I_T&=I_{T\cup S}-I_S=3-(7)=-4,\\I_U&=I_R-I_{T\cup S}=0-(3)=-3.
\end{aligned}
$$

Apply the piecewise weights and linearity:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\iint_{R} g(x,y)\,\mathrm{d}A&=-3I_T+(2)I_U\\&=-3(-4)+(2)(-3)\\&=6.
\end{aligned}
$$

The zero branch on $S$ contributes nothing.

Write $I_E=\iint_{E} f(x,y)\,\mathrm{d}A$ for any subregion $E$. By additivity, recover the missing contributions:

$$
\begin{aligned}
I_S&=I_{S\cup U}-I_U=-7-(-2)=-5,\\I_T&=I_R-I_{S\cup U}=-3-(-7)=4.
\end{aligned}
$$

Apply the piecewise weights and linearity:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\iint_{R} g(x,y)\,\mathrm{d}A&=2I_S+(3)I_T\\&=2(-5)+(3)(4)\\&=2.
\end{aligned}
$$

The zero branch on $U$ contributes nothing.

Write $I_E=\iint_{E} f(x,y)\,\mathrm{d}A$ for any subregion $E$. By additivity, recover the missing contributions:

$$
\begin{aligned}
I_U&=I_{U\cup T}-I_T=5-(-3)=8,\\I_S&=I_R-I_{U\cup T}=11-(5)=6.
\end{aligned}
$$

Apply the piecewise weights and linearity:

$$
\begin{aligned}
\iint_{R} g(x,y)\,\mathrm{d}A&=3I_U+(-2)I_S\\&=3(8)+(-2)(6)\\&=12.
\end{aligned}
$$

The zero branch on $T$ contributes nothing.
